            <ArticleTitle>Isolated left atrial appendage ostial stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>702-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/ejechocard/jep060</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with atrial tachycardia presented with dyspnoea on exertion. Transoesophageal echocardiography revealed idiopathic left atrial appendage stenosis. The mouth of the atrial appendage was narrowed, and there was a high velocity to and fro jet between the left atrial body and the left atrial appendage. The study, therefore, suggested isolated left atrial appendage orifice stenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
